      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:3:4:20:3",
      "text": [
        " أَدْنَى مَا يُجْزِئُ مِنَ التَّكْبِيرِ فِي التَّوَجُّهِ تَكْبِيرَةٌ وَاحِدَةٌ وَ ثَلَاثُ تَكْبِيرَاتٍ أَحْسَنُ وَ سَبْعٌ أَفْضَلُ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "From him, from his father, from Hammad Bin Isa, from Hareyz, from Zurara who said, ",
          "‘The lowest of what would suffice from the exclamation of <span class=\"iTxt\">Takbīr</span> during the direction, is one <span class=\"iTxt\">Takbīr</span>; and three <span class=\"iTxt\">Takbīr</span>s are better, and seven would be superior’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "3. It is a narration from him (narrator of previous Hadith) by his father Hammad ibn ‘Isa from Hariz from Zurarah who has said the following: “He (the Imam), ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said, ‘The least for Takbir (Allah is great beyond description) facing (al-Qiblah (al-Ka‘bah)) is to say it once. Three times is good and seven times is better.”’ "
        ]
      }
